#{[17592186482702 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186482685 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186482702 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186482701 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186482702 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186482702 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(-2,3)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(3,-1)$ and $(6, 5)$. Write your answer in **standard form.** Use $Ax+By=C$ with integer $A,B,C$, $A>0$, and coprime $A$ and $B$ (their greatest common divisor is $1$). Enter $Ax+By$ in the first blank and $C$ in the second blank.\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=$\n{{field-2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186482702 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e25fd592-804a-557b-ae2e-2341670e35ba" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186482702 #edb/ref 1074 "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(3,-1)$ and $(6,5)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m &= \\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1} \\\\ &= \\frac{5-(-1)}{6-(3)} \\\\ &= 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of $2$ and passes through the point $(-2,3)$. To find the equation of this line, we use point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1 &= m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(3) &= 2(x-(-2)) \\\\ y-(3) &= 2 x + 4 \\\\ y &= 2 x + 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, write the equation in standard form with coprime integer coefficients and a positive $x$-coefficient.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2 x + 7 \\\\ 2 x -y &= -7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first blank is $2 x -y$ and the second blank is $-7$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186482708 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186175912.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186482708 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "f306f06a-785e-5d4c-bd17-02ca8cc6dc42" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186485752 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186486467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485752 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186486475 #edb/ref 175921860454